      "textEn": "Contemplated by the union with the supreme self, by the unveiling of the supreme, by the supreme religion, by the opening of the door, the mind is covered.\nIn the world of the self, you have attained the experience of your own happiness. 33. Meaning of the word\n\nOm—Oh God; Namah—Greetings; Te—To you; Astu—Yes; Bhagavan—Oh Lord; Narayan—Dwelling of all souls,\nNarayan; Vasudev—Lord Vasudev, Shri Krishna; the first-born—the first-born; the great-born—the great-born; the great-experiencer—\nThe supremely glorious; the supremely auspicious; the supremely benevolent; the supremely compassionate;\nThe compassionate; the unchanging; the sustainer of the universe—the support of the visible world; the lord of the world—of all the worlds;\nThe lord of the supremely ascetic, who wanders in all the worlds; the supreme—extreme; the self-yoga-samadhin—engaged in devotion;\nThe pervaded—extremely pure; the manifest—and fully revealed; Para-himsacharana—the performance of the divine law of loving-kindness;\nInaugurated—opened; Tamah—of ignorance; Kapat—in which the door; Dware—located at the door; Chitte—in the mind; Apavrute—\nWithout impurity; Atma-loka—in the self-world; Swayam—self; Avlokit—by experiencing; Nija—own, of oneself;\nSukha-Anubhava—experience of happiness; Bhavan—you. Hey Bhagavan, Hey Narayan, Hey Vasudev, Hey original being, supreme experience, direct auspiciousness! Hey supreme\nBlessing form, extremely merciful and unchangeable! Hey, the basis of this visible world, Hey, all the people,\nAnd the master of every object, and the husband of Lakshmi Devi! Only the best of ascetics can interview you,\nwho, being completely absorbed in meditation in devotion, preach the essence of Krishna consciousness throughout the world. They keep their attention focused on themselves, therefore, in their pure\ninner self, they accept your form. When the darkness of their hearts is completely\nremoved, and you have a vision, then they attain the divine bliss of your divine form.\nBesides such individuals, no one else can experience you, therefore we\nSalute you with respect. Meaning: According to various types of interviews, devotees and divine sages have given Shri Bhagavan\ntheir own many divine names. When they are experienced in a formless state,\nthey are called Parabrahma. When they are experienced as the Supreme Soul, they are called Antarayami.\nAnd when they expand in various forms for the material creation, they are called Kshirodakshayi Vishnu,\nGarbhodakshayi Vishnu, and Karanodakshayi Vishnu. When they experienced him in the form of Chaturvyuha—Vasudeva,\nSankarshana, Pradyumna, and Aniruddha—who are beyond the said three forms of Vishnu"
